  "final_message": "I have run the directory listing command and will check the output once it completes.\nI have started searching for `channel` references across the codebase.\nWaiting for the search to complete.\nI will check git status to verify current repository state.\nI will wait for the search to complete.\nI am waiting for the file search to complete.\nI am listing the repository files.\nI am waiting for the file listing task to complete.\nI will pause tool calls to allow the background task to complete.\nI have run `npm test` and will inspect the output when it completes.\nI will stop calling tools while `npm test` runs.\nI am now waiting for `npm test` to complete.\nI am waiting for the command to finish.\nI cannot drop `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Reasons:\n\n1. **Cross-Repository Consumers**: Even if the field is not read locally within `orders-service`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to downstream services in other repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n2. **Additive Changes Only**: Under ARCH-4, changes to published events must be additive. Outright removal of a field is a breaking change for downstream consumers.\n3. **Deprecation Process Required**: Field removals and renames must go through a formal deprecation cycle (such as marking `channel` deprecated, coordinating removal with downstream consumers, and bumping schema versions) rather than being deleted directly.\n",
